      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T00:41:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Table 30-1 from the IPMI Spec lists 6 mandatory commands if PEF or Alerting is supported. Arm PEF Postpone Timer, Set Last Processed Event ID and Get Last Processed Event ID.\nThe PEF postpone timer allows the system a window to handle a event before PEF act on it, and also allows to disable the PEF during runtime (IPMI spec section 30.2). And with the set/get last processed event ID it handles pending events across BMC reset.\nI think these should be in scope for this document.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "3451089e9146dc04a1dae9535ee3cce27a6ddeed",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6eb12eed_e4cfa9ba",
        "filename": "designs/platform-event-filtering.md",
